I understand exactly why this is happening. The issue is in your **VoucherCommandService.java** in the logWorkflowAction call inside the createBatchRequest method.
Right now, you are passing dto.getScheduledTime() into logWorkflowAction, but your history logic in the UI is not rendering it because it defaults to "Immediate Execution" if it doesn't see a specifically formatted keyword in the action string.
### The Fix
#### 1. Update VoucherCommandService.java
You need to make sure the "Submitted" action string explicitly contains the scheduling information so the history log chip knows to render it.
Find this line in your createBatchRequest method:
```java
workflowEngine.logWorkflowAction(batchId, dto.getVid(), "Submitted", creatorId, dto.getCommonBatchRemarks(), dto.getScheduledTime());

```
**Change it to this:**
```java
// Pass the scheduled time, and ensure the action string hints at the schedule
String action = (dto.getScheduledTime() != null) ? "Submitted (Scheduled)" : "Submitted";
workflowEngine.logWorkflowAction(batchId, dto.getVid(), action, creatorId, dto.getCommonBatchRemarks(), dto.getScheduledTime());

```
#### 2. Update VoucherPostingStatus.jsx (History Map Logic)
Now, update your history mapping loop one last time. We need to make sure it respects the history.SCHEDULED_TIME for the "Submitted" action.
Replace your workflowHistory.map logic with this:
```javascript
{workflowHistory.map((history, idx) => {
    // ... (keep your existing const definitions for userName, initial, etc)

    const rawAction = history.LAST_ACTION || "System Action";
    const cleanAction = rawAction.replace(/\s*\(.*?\)\s*/g, '').trim();
    
    const isSubmission = rawAction.toUpperCase().includes("SUBMIT");
    const isScheduled = rawAction.toUpperCase().includes("(SCHEDULED)"); // Matches our new string!

    return (
        // ... inside your Stack ...
        <Stack direction="row" spacing={1} alignItems="center" sx={{ mb: 1.5, flexWrap: "wrap", gap: 1 }}>
            <Chip label={cleanAction} size="small" ... />

            {/* If it was submitted as scheduled, show the chip */}
            {(isSubmission && isScheduled && history.SCHEDULED_TIME) ? (
                <Chip 
                    label={`Scheduled for: ${formatDateTime(history.SCHEDULED_TIME)}`} 
                    size="small" 
                    color="info" 
                    variant="outlined" 
                    sx={jaStyles.historySchedChip} 
                />
            ) : isSubmission ? (
                <Chip label="Immediate Execution" size="small" color="default" variant="outlined" sx={{ ...jaStyles.historySchedChip, backgroundColor: "#f1f5f9" }} />
            ) : null}
            
            {/* ... keep your existing Final Approval logic ... */}
        </Stack>
    );
})}

```
### Why this works:
 1. **Action String Hint:** By changing the action string to "Submitted (Scheduled)", the React code can now clearly distinguish between a standard submission and a scheduled one.
 2. **Explicit Data Binding:** By using history.SCHEDULED_TIME (which comes directly from the database row for that history event), it will always show the time the creator selected, and it will **never** be overwritten by a Final Approver's later actions because that history row is immutable.
Apply these two changes, and your Status screen will correctly display the Creator's scheduled time for the "Submitted" event!
